      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'll start you on atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. You take it by mouth. That should help with cardiovascular risk. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Please don't stop the blood thinner on your own, even if you feel fine. Cardiac rehab is worth doing, it really helps your confidence.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:16",
      "end_timestamp": "04:36",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
